  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Piva and associates conducted a study on the intertester reliability of knee flexion ROM measurements using an inclinometer in patients with patellofemoral pain syndrome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Piva and associates conducted a study on the reliability of the Ely test for knee flexion ROM using an inclinometer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Researchers who measured knee flexion ROM using an inclinometer in patients with patellofemoral pain syndrome."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-90aa2c67eee53a88d282d9e6987ca28b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-907485f01764ad42a85685e6e4a21163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a7abf467a8b1da896b788e651526495</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DUCHENNE MUSCULAR DYSTROPHY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A genetic disorder characterized by progressive muscle degeneration and weakness, often affecting children."&lt;SEP&gt;"Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy is a genetic disorder characterized by progressive muscle degeneration and weakness, affecting the range of motion in joints like the knee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-90aa2c67eee53a88d282d9e6987ca28b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-950c58b7df97a4bc1fdeb2087de52f18</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPASTIC CEREBRAL PALSY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A type of cerebral palsy characterized by increased muscle tone and stiffness, often affecting movement and posture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spastic Cerebral Palsy is a type of cerebral palsy characterized by increased muscle tone and stiffness, affecting the range of motion in joints like the knee."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spastic cerebral palsy is a condition characterized by muscle stiffness and difficulty with movement, often affecting children."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-90aa2c67eee53a88d282d9e6987ca28b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-950c58b7df97a4bc1fdeb2087de52f18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a7abf467a8b1da896b788e651526495</data>
</node>
