</node>
<node id="&quot;RADIOGRAPHS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Imaging technique used to evaluate the knee ROM of 21 healthy volunteers, providing visual data for analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging technique used to validate goniometric measurements of knee joint angles, providing a gold standard for comparison."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiographs are imaging techniques used to validate knee joint angle measurements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiographs are imaging techniques used to visualize the internal structures of the knee, particularly for validating goniometric measurements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiographs, or X-rays, are used in conjunction with goniometers to measure knee ROM accurately."&lt;SEP&gt;"X-ray images used to validate knee joint angle measurements in the study by Gogia and colleagues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a7abf467a8b1da896b788e651526495&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90aa2c67eee53a88d282d9e6987ca28b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d86601906259a5a5da4abf14e4637db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-907485f01764ad42a85685e6e4a21163</data>
</node>
