  <data key="d2">chunk-907485f01764ad42a85685e6e4a21163</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLEFFKEN AND ASSOCIATES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cleffken and associates conducted a study on the intratester and intertester reproducibility of knee flexion and extension measurements using an electronic digital inclinometer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cleffken and associates studied the intratester and intertester reproducibility of knee flexion and extension measurements using an electronic digital inclinometer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a7abf467a8b1da896b788e651526495&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-907485f01764ad42a85685e6e4a21163</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PIRIYAPRASARTH AND COLLEAGUES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Piriyaprasarth and colleagues assessed the intratester and intertester reliability of knee measurements using a flexible electrogoniometer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Piriyaprasarth and colleagues conducted a study on the intratester and intertester reliability of measurements using a flexible electrogoniometer at different fixed flexion angles and body positions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a7abf467a8b1da896b788e651526495&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-907485f01764ad42a85685e6e4a21163</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BENNETT AND COLLEAGUES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bennett and colleagues evaluated the reliability and validity of digital imaging and photography for measuring knee ROM."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-907485f01764ad42a85685e6e4a21163</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NAYLOR AND ASSOCIATES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Naylor and associates evaluated the validity and reliability of measuring knee ROM using a goniometer in conjunction with radiographs and photographs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Naylor and associates evaluated the validity of measuring ROM from photographs referenced to radiographs, finding excellent validity for flexion but less for extension."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-907485f01764ad42a85685e6e4a21163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCLINOMETER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Inclinometer is a device used to measure angles of inclination or slope, often used in physical therapy to assess joint movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"An inclinometer is a device used to measure angles of tilt, slope, or elevation, often used in medical studies to measure knee flexion and extension."&lt;SEP&gt;"An inclinometer is a device used to measure angles of tilt, slope, or inclination, often compared to goniometers in measuring knee flexion."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d86601906259a5a5da4abf14e4637db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a7abf467a8b1da896b788e651526495&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-907485f01764ad42a85685e6e4a21163</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLEURIMETER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A pleurimeter is a device used to measure the range of motion (ROM) of the knee, typically attached to the lower leg for precise measurements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-907485f01764ad42a85685e6e4a21163</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CYBEX ED1320&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The CYBEX ED1320 is an electronic digital inclinometer used to measure knee flexion and extension in a study by Cleffken and associates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-907485f01764ad42a85685e6e4a21163</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FLEXIBLE ELECTROGONIOMETER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A flexible electrogoniometer is a device used to measure joint angles and is particularly useful for measuring knee flexion and extension in various positions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-907485f01764ad42a85685e6e4a21163</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIGITAL IMAGING AND PHOTOGRAPHY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Digital imaging and photography techniques are used to measure knee range of motion (ROM) without relying on skin marks or bony landmarks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-907485f01764ad42a85685e6e4a21163</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARKER METHOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"METHOD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The marker method involves placing a skin marker on the greater trochanter to align the goniometer for measuring knee ROM."&lt;SEP&gt;"The marker method involves using a skin marker on the greater trochanter to align the goniometer for measuring knee ROM."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-907485f01764ad42a85685e6e4a21163</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LINE OF FEMUR METHOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"METHOD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The line of femur method involves estimating the line of the femur to align the goniometer for measuring knee ROM."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-907485f01764ad42a85685e6e4a21163</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRTY-ONE VOLUNTEERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Thirty-one volunteers, consisting of 13 with arthritis and 18 healthy participants, were examined in a study comparing methods of goniometer alignment for measuring knee ROM."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THREE EXAMINERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Three examiners conducted the examinations using both the marker method and the line of femur method to measure knee ROM."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF PITTSBURGH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The University of Pittsburgh is where Tsai and colleagues developed the Rotameter, a device for measuring passive internal and external rotation at the knee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ROTAMETER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Rotameter is a device developed at the University of Pittsburgh to measure passive internal and external rotation at the knee, consisting of a foam walker boot with a force/moment sensor and a magnetic tracking system."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ROTTAMETER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Rottameter is an external device used to measure knee rotation, tested by Almquist and colleagues, with varying reliability depending on the applied torque and knee flexion angles."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COACHES EYE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Coaches Eye is a two-dimensional motion-analysis tablet app used to assess sagittal plane kinematics during the FMS deep squat, providing reliable measurements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FMS (FUNCTIONAL MOVEMENT SYSTEM)">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"FMS is a battery of seven fundamental movement tests used to evaluate and categorize functional movement patterns."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TSAI AND COLLEAGUES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tsai and colleagues developed the Rotameter and tested its reliability for measuring knee rotation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KRAUSE AND COLLEAGUES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Krause and colleagues studied the reliability of the Coaches Eye app for goniometric assessment of sagittal plane hip, knee, and ankle motion during the FMS deep squat."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIGITAL PHOTOGRAPHS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Digital photographs are used as a method to measure knee motion, showing higher intraobserver reliability compared to traditional goniometry."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLASTIC 360-DEGREE UG WITH 20-CENTIMETER ARMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A plastic 360-degree universal goniometer with 20-centimeter arms, used as a traditional method to measure knee motion."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VICON MOTION-ANALYSIS PROGRAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Vicon motion-analysis program is a 3D system used to measure range of motion, providing a comparison to the Coaches Eye app."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FMS (FUNCTIONAL MOVEMENT SYSTEM) DEEP SQUAT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The FMS deep squat is a test within the Functional Movement System used to evaluate functional movement patterns, specifically focusing on the deep squat maneuver."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAGITTAL PLANE HIP, KNEE, AND ANKLE MOTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sagittal plane hip, knee, and ankle motion refers to the movements of these joints in the sagittal plane, which is a plane that divides the body into left and right halves."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTRARATER RELIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Intrarater Reliability refers to the consistency of measurements taken by the same person at different times, often evaluated using intraclass correlation coefficients (ICCs)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intrarater reliability refers to the consistency of measurements taken by the same examiner over time."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERRATER RELIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interrater reliability refers to the consistency of measurements taken by different examiners."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONCORDANCE CORRELATION COEFFICIENTS (CCCS)">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Concordance correlation coefficients (CCCs) are statistical measures used to assess the agreement between two sets of measurements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STANDARD GONIOMETRY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Standard goniometry is the traditional method of measuring joint angles using a goniometer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PHOTOGRAPHY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Photography is used as a method to provide a permanent record of measurements, offering greater transparency and opportunities to confer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEAN DIFFERENCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mean differences refer to the average difference between two sets of measurements, indicating the level of agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;95% LIMITS OF AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"95% limits of agreement are a statistical measure indicating the range within which the true difference between two measurements is likely to lie."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTRAOBSERVER SEM (STANDARD ERROR OF MEASUREMENT)">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Intraobserver SEM is a measure of the variability of measurements taken by the same observer, indicating the precision of the measurements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTEROBSERVER RELIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interobserver reliability refers to the consistency of measurements taken by different observers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MDC (MINIMAL DETECTABLE CHANGE)">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"MDC is the smallest change in a measurement that can be detected with a certain level of confidence, indicating the sensitivity of the measurement tool."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KNEE ANGLES OF 30 AND 90 DEGREES OF KNEE FLEXION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Knee angles of 30 and 90 degrees of knee flexion are specific positions of the knee joint used in the measurement of passive internal and external rotation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;11 SUBJECTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Eleven subjects were tested using the Rotameter to measure passive internal and external rotation at the knee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;10 HEALTHY ADULTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ten healthy adults were tested using the Rottameter to measure knee rotation, with measurements taken in the morning and afternoon of the same day."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANOTHER GROUP OF 10 FEMALES AND MALES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Another group of 10 females and males were tested using the Rottameter to measure knee rotation, with measurements taken 1 week apart."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;10 VOLUNTEERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"10 volunteers participated in the study conducted by Desloovere and colleagues, performing various motor tasks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ten volunteers were measured by Desloeree and colleagues to assess knee joint motion in three anatomical planes during various motor tasks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIDESTEP TURN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sidestep turn is a motor task that showed significantly larger knee joint rotations compared to standard walking."&lt;SEP&gt;"The sidestep turn is a motor task where knee joint rotations were significantly larger than during standard walking."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DESCENDING A STEP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Descending a step is a motor task that showed significantly larger knee joint rotations compared to standard walking."&lt;SEP&gt;"Descending a step is a motor task where knee joint rotations were significantly larger than during standard walking."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STANDARD WALKING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Standard walking is a baseline motor task used for comparison in the study of knee joint motion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Standard walking is a baseline motor task used for comparison in the study."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07ca63fd10cfd76d8fe746402f8a6481</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KNEE AXIAL ROTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Knee axial rotation is a type of knee joint movement that was found to increase significantly during turning tasks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JENNY92&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Jenny92 used a smartphone application to measure knee flexion angles during total knee arthroplasties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TOTAL KNEE ARTHROPLASTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Total knee arthroplasties are surgical procedures performed on patients with end-stage knee osteoarthritis."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;END-STAGE KNEE OSTEOARTHRITIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"End-stage knee osteoarthritis is a condition affecting the knee joints of the patients in the study."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SMARTPHONE APPLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A smartphone application was used to measure knee flexion angles, showing significant correlation with navigated measurements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NAVIGATED SYSTEM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A navigated system was used to measure knee flexion angles, providing a reference for comparison with smartphone measurements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCKENDON AND GILBERT93&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ockendon and Gilbert93 compared a smartphone accelerometer-based knee goniometer with a conventional goniometer for assessing fixed knee deformities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SMARTPHONE GONIOMETER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A smartphone goniometer is a device used to measure knee flexion, showing high reliability in the study."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONVENTIONAL GONIOMETER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A conventional goniometer is a traditional tool used to measure knee flexion, used as a reference in the study."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FERRIEREO AND COLLEAGUES94&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ferriereo and colleagues94 assessed the reliability of a smartphone-based application (Dr. Goniometer) for measuring knee joint angles."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DR. GONIOMETER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dr. Goniometer is a smartphone application used for photographic-based goniometry, showing high reliability in the study."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOGIA AND COLLEAGUES75&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gogia and colleagues75 measured knee joint angles and validated these measurements with radiographs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENWEMEKA79&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Enwemeka79 compared UG measurements with bone angle measurements provided by radiographs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ERSOZ AND ERGUN37&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ersoz and Ergun37 used a UG to measure knee joint angles, providing further validation of the measurements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;11 MOTOR TASKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"11 motor tasks were performed by volunteers in the study conducted by Desloovere and colleagues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;4 MEN AND 6 WOMEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"4 men and 6 women were the patients undergoing total knee arthroplasties in Jenny92's study."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEAN AGE OF 69 YEARS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The mean age of the patients in Jenny92's study was 69 years."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;5 HEALTHY MALES AGED 30 TO 40 YEARS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"5 healthy males aged 30 to 40 years participated in the study conducted by Ockendon and Gilbert93."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;10 HEALTHY ADULT VOLUNTEERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">|&gt;"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"10 healthy adult volunteers (4 women and 6 men) participated in the study conducted by Enwemeka79."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;4 WOMEN AND 6 MEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"4 women and 6 men were the healthy adult volunteers in Enwemeka79's study."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;35 PHOTOGRAPHS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">|&gt;"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"35 photographs of knee flexion angles were used in the study conducted by Ferriereo and colleagues94."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIX POSITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">|&gt;"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Six positions of the knee were measured in Jenny92's study, starting at full extension and ending at maximal flexion."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIX RATERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">|&gt;"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Six raters performed repeated measurements with both the smartphone app and the UG in Ferriereo and colleagues94's study."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8823385d2274c1cb6b908f4fb041f76c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;10 OTHER RATERS&quot;">
