<node id="&quot;KNEE OSTEOARTHRITIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A medical condition characterized by the deterioration of cartilage in the knee joint, affecting mobility and causing pain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knee Osteoarthritis is a condition characterized by the deterioration of the knee joint, often studied in terms of its impact on range of motion and radiographic findings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knee osteoarthritis is a condition characterized by the deterioration of the cartilage in the knee joint, leading to pain and reduced mobility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d86601906259a5a5da4abf14e4637db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56ba6457f7a7f43d803a693f91176eca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PASSIVE KNEE EXTENSION TEST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Passive Knee Extension Test is a method used to measure the length of the hamstring muscles, evaluating the range of motion during passive movement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HAMSTRING MUSCLE LENGTH (HML)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hamstring Muscle Length (HML) is a measure of the flexibility of the hamstring muscles, often assessed using passive straight leg raise and popliteal angle measurements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARALLELOGRAM GONIOMETER (PG)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
