  <data key="d2">chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIBIOFEMORAL COMPARTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A part of the knee joint, specifically the area where the tibia and femur meet, often assessed in studies of knee osteoarthritis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tibiofemoral Compartment is a part of the knee joint where the tibia and femur articulate, often assessed in studies of knee osteoarthritis."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d86601906259a5a5da4abf14e4637db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LATERAL TIBIOFEMORAL COMPARTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A specific part of the tibia-femur joint, often assessed for signs of osteoarthritis and related conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lateral Tibiofemoral Compartment is a specific area within the tibiofemoral compartment, often assessed for signs of osteoarthritis."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d86601906259a5a5da4abf14e4637db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LATERAL KNEE COMPARTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A specific part of the knee joint, often assessed for signs of osteoarthritis and related conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRITERION VALIDITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A measure of how well a test or measurement correlates with a gold standard, often used to validate the accuracy of ROM measurements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Criterion Validity is a measure of how well a test or measurement tool correlates with a gold standard, such as radiographic measurements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d86601906259a5a5da4abf14e4637db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PEARSON PRODUCT MOMENT CORRELATION COEFFICIENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A statistical measure used to determine the strength and direction of the relationship between two variables, often used in validity studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pearson Product Moment Correlation Coefficients are statistical measures used to determine the strength and direction of the relationship between two variables."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d86601906259a5a5da4abf14e4637db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTRACLASS CORRELATION COEFFICIENTS (ICCS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A statistical measure used to assess the reliability of measurements, particularly in studies involving repeated measures by the same rater."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRUNK–THIGH ANGLE (PSLR)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A measure of the angle between the trunk and thigh, often used to assess hamstring muscle length and flexibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POPLITEAL ANGLE (PA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A measure of the angle between the thigh and leg, often used to assess hamstring muscle length and flexibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STANDARD ERRORS OF MEASUREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A statistical measure that indicates the precision of a measurement, often used to evaluate the reliability of tests."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SMALLEST DETECTABLE DIFFERENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A measure that indicates the smallest change in a measurement that can be detected with confidence, often used to evaluate the sensitivity of tests."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-704af454e8435279b724980dccc9f577</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KNEE FLEXION CONTRACTURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
