  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FERREIRO, G, ET AL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Authors of a study on the reliability of a smartphone-based goniometer for knee goniometry."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF REHABILITATION RESEARCH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A journal that published a study on the reliability of a smartphone-based goniometer for knee goniometry."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KNEE RANGE OF MOTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The extent of movement possible at the knee joint, including flexion, extension, and rotation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIBIAL CONDYLES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The two concave surfaces on the proximal end of the tibia that articulate with the femoral condyles."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDIAL COLLATERAL LIGAMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A ligament that provides medial-lateral stability to the knee, located on the inner side of the joint."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ILIOTIBIAL BAND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A thick band of fibrous tissue that runs along the outer side of the leg, providing medial-lateral stability to the knee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KNEE FLEXORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Muscles that help to bend the knee, providing posterior stability to the joint."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANTERIOR CRUCIATE LIGAMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A ligament within the knee joint that prevents the tibia from sliding forward relative to the femur, providing stability during rotational movements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POSTERIOR CRUCIATE LIGAMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A ligament within the knee joint that prevents the tibia from sliding backward relative to the femur, providing stability during rotational movements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSVERSE PLANE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A plane that divides the body into upper and lower sections, where rotational movements occur."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VERTICAL AXIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An axis running from top to bottom through the knee, around which rotational movements occur."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PASSIVE RANGE OF MOTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The range of movement that can be achieved without voluntary muscle contraction, typically measured by an external force."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACTIVE RANGE OF MOTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The range of movement that can be achieved through voluntary muscle contraction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-WEIGHT-BEARING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A condition where the knee is not supporting the body's weight, often used in clinical assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WEIGHT-BEARING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A condition where the knee supports the body's weight, often used in clinical assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;YOUNG CHILDREN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A demographic group characterized by a greater range of knee extension compared to adults."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efbffe4c52beae140acaca62d94996bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HAYES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hayes is a researcher who reported a mean ratio of extension loss to flexion loss in a study of patients with osteoarthritis."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OSTEOARTHRITIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Osteoarthritis is a degenerative joint disease that affects the cartilage and bones within a joint, often leading to pain and reduced mobility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTHRITIS OR ARTHROSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arthritis or Arthroses refers to conditions involving inflammation or degeneration of joints, which can affect the knee and lead to pain and limited movement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RANGE OF MOTION TESTING PROCEDURES: KNEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Range of Motion Testing Procedures for the knee involve specific methods to measure the extent of movement at the knee joint, including flexion, extension, and rotation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GONIOMETER ALIGNMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Goniometer Alignment is a technique used in range of motion testing to accurately measure the angles of joint movement, particularly at the knee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FLEXION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Flexion is a type of movement at the knee joint, characterized by bending the leg at the knee, bringing the heel closer to the buttock."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flexion is the movement of the knee joint that decreases the angle between the thigh and the lower leg."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d86601906259a5a5da4abf14e4637db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PASSIVE RANGE OF MOTION (PROM)">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Passive Range of Motion (PROM) refers to the range of movement at the knee joint when the movement is performed by an external force, such as a therapist, without the patient's active muscle effort."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot; EXAMINER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Examiner is the person conducting the range of motion tests, responsible for aligning the goniometer and assessing the movement of the knee joint."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBJECT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Subject is the person whose knee is being measured for range of motion, often lying supine or in another specified position during the test."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHENG AND COLLEAGUES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cheng and colleagues studied 2360 Chinese children and found that the average knee extension beyond 0 degrees decreased from 16 degrees at age 3 to 7 degrees by age 9."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ef81e2a2ef718984fd40ce92806308f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LATERAL MIDLINE OF THE FIBULA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">| "CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lateral Midline of the Fibula is a reference line used for aligning the distal arm of the goniometer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ef81e2a2ef718984fd40ce92806308f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FLEXION CONTRACTURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Flexion Contractures refer to the condition where the knee or hip cannot fully extend, often associated with increased disability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ef81e2a2ef718984fd40ce92806308f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIP EXTENSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hip Extension is a movement of the hip joint, which, along with knee flexion, is strongly related to disability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ef81e2a2ef718984fd40ce92806308f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LATERAL ROTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lateral Rotation is a movement of the hip joint, which, along with knee flexion and hip extension, is strongly related to disability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ef81e2a2ef718984fd40ce92806308f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRIMARY KNEE OSTEOARTHRITIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Primary Knee Osteoarthritis is a condition affecting the knee joint, often resulting in extension limitations and reduced mobility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ef81e2a2ef718984fd40ce92806308f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEALTHY MALE VOLUNTEERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Healthy Male Volunteers are individuals aged 15 to 73 years who participated in a study examining age-related changes in the hip and knee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ef81e2a2ef718984fd40ce92806308f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIVINGSTON AND ASSOCIATES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Livingston and associates used different staircase dimensions to measure knee flexion range, finding that shorter subjects had a greater maximum mean knee flexion range for stair ascent."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-80cc1aeca75db3a2a6be0a84bff43fd8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KNEE FLEXION RANGE OF MOTION (ROM)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Knee flexion ROM is the range of motion in the knee joint during flexion, which varies by age, gender, and body mass index."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-80cc1aeca75db3a2a6be0a84bff43fd8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GENDER DIFFERENCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gender differences in knee ROM and joint laxity, with females generally having more joint laxity and greater knee flexion ROM than males."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-80cc1aeca75db3a2a6be0a84bff43fd8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OBESITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Obesity is a condition characterized by excess body fat, which can affect knee ROM and increase the risk of knee pain or stiffness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-80cc1aeca75db3a2a6be0a84bff43fd8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;76 RIGHT KNEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"76 right knees were classified as having an abnormal (limited) passive ROM in flexion based on the criterion of not reaching 124 degrees of flexion."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-80cc1aeca75db3a2a6be0a84bff43fd8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;63 LEFT KNEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"63 left knees were classified as having an abnormal (limited) passive ROM in flexion based on the criterion of not reaching 124 degrees of flexion."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-80cc1aeca75db3a2a6be0a84bff43fd8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1081 MALES AND FEMALES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"1081 males and females were studied by Beighton, Solomon, and Soskolne to define joint laxity, including knee hyperextension."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-80cc1aeca75db3a2a6be0a84bff43fd8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;10 FEMALE PATIENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"10 female patients diagnosed with hypermobility syndrome were studied by Hall and colleagues to examine alterations in proprioceptive acuity at the knee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-80cc1aeca75db3a2a6be0a84bff43fd8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;5042 POST OFFICE PENSIONERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">| "CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"5042 Post Office pensioners were surveyed by Sobti and colleagues to examine the association between obesity and knee pain or stiffness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-80cc1aeca75db3a2a6be0a84bff43fd8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;33 YOUNG HEALTHY MALE AND FEMALE SUBJECTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">| "CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"33 young healthy male and female subjects ranging in age from 18 to 39 years were studied by Protopapadaki and associates to measure knee motion during stair ascent and descent."&lt;SEP&gt;"A group of 33 young healthy individuals ranging in age from 18 to 39 years, used in a study to determine knee motion during stair ascent and descent."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-80cc1aeca75db3a2a6be0a84bff43fd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c052988db1f3bec75acfc56a5c3d59</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WINTER40&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Winter40 is a reference to a study or researcher, mentioned in the context of stair dimensions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1c052988db1f3bec75acfc56a5c3d59</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;20 ELDERLY SUBJECTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
