  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
  <data key="d1">"The knee joint is capable of extension, which is the straightening movement that moves the heel away from the buttock."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTHROKINEMATICS&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arthrokinematics describes the movement of the knee joint surfaces, including the sliding and rolling of the femoral and tibial condyles during flexion and extension."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WEIGHT-BEARING FLEXION&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
  <data key="d1">"Weight-bearing flexion of the knee involves bending the joint while supporting the weight of the body, which is important for functional activities."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WEIGHT-BEARING EXTENSION&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
  <data key="d1">"Weight-bearing extension of the knee involves straightening the joint while supporting the weight of the body, which is important for functional activities."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIGH&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
  <data key="d1">"The thigh is the upper part of the leg, containing important muscles and bones such as the femur, which are crucial for knee joint function."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEG&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
  <data key="d1">"The leg is the lower part of the limb, containing important bones such as the tibia and fibula, which are crucial for knee joint function."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FEMORAL CONDYLES&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
  <data key="d1">"The femoral condyles are the rounded ends of the femur that articulate with the tibia to form the knee joint, allowing for movements such as flexion and extension."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDIAL FEMORAL CONDYLE&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
  <data key="d1">"The medial femoral condyle is the inner rounded end of the femur that articulates with the tibia to form part of the knee joint."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LATERAL FEMORAL CONDYLE&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
  <data key="d1">"The lateral femoral condyle is the outer rounded end of the femur that articulates with the tibia to form part of the knee joint."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STABILIZATION&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
  <data key="d1">"Stabilization is the process of keeping the femur stable during range of motion testing to ensure accurate measurement and prevent unwanted movements."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STARTING POSITION&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
  <data key="d1">"The starting position is the initial posture or alignment of the body and limbs before performing a range of motion test, ensuring consistency and accuracy in the measurement."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXAMINER&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-6854c72d0616470d858bc189ee907e36</data>
  <data key="d1">"The examiner is responsible for aligning the goniometer and assessing the movement of the subject's knee joint, ensuring accurate and consistent measurements."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
