<edge source="&quot;HIP&quot;" target="&quot;HIP IMPINGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d3">9.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Pain during hip flexion can indicate hip impingement, a condition where there are structural abnormalities in the hip joint.</data>
  <data key="d5">"pain, joint condition"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7f7944fa53271cc7aa6b58f4001aaa11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HIP&quot;" target="&quot;HIP CONTRACTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d3">9.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Limited range of motion in the hip can indicate hip contracture, often due to scar tissue or muscle tightness.</data>
  <data key="d5">"movement limitation, joint condition"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7f7944fa53271cc7aa6b58f4001aaa11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HIP&quot;" target="&quot;HIP INSTABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d3">9.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Asymmetry in abduction and adduction movements can indicate hip instability, leading to potential joint issues.</data>
  <data key="d5">"movement asymmetry, joint stability"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7f7944fa53271cc7aa6b58f4001aaa11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HIP&quot;" target="&quot;HIP ARTHRITIS&quot;">
  <data key="d3">9.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Reduced range of motion in adduction movements can indicate hip arthritis, a condition where the hip joint is inflamed.</data>
  <data key="d5">"movement limitation, joint inflammation"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7f7944fa53271cc7aa6b58f4001aaa11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HIP&quot;" target="&quot;FAI SYNDROME&quot;">
  <data key="d3">9.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Limited internal rotation in the hip joint can indicate femoroacetabular impingement syndrome (FAI syndrome).</data>
  <data key="d5">"movement limitation, joint condition"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7f7944fa53271cc7aa6b58f4001aaa11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HIP&quot;" target="&quot;ELY TEST&quot;">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The Ely test requires the hip to be positioned in 0 degrees of flexion to accurately measure the length of the rectus femoris muscle."</data>
  <data key="d5">"positioning, joint stability"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aebf522eb13809f43facec9b7c1f746</data>
</edge>
