  <data key="d5">"flexion, measurement"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aebf522eb13809f43facec9b7c1f746</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;KNEE&quot;" target="&quot;HAMSTRING MUSCLES&quot;">
  <data key="d3">16.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The hamstring muscles are a group of muscles in the posterior thigh, including the semimembranosus, semitendinosus, and biceps femoris, that contribute to knee flexion and help stabilize the knee joint."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hamstring muscles are responsible for flexing the knee, and their length is assessed through various tests, including the Ely test."</data>
  <data key="d5">"muscle function, joint movement"&lt;SEP&gt;"muscle function, joint stability"</data>
